.\" robodr-spool-export(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-export/src/bin/robodr-spool-export.rs and the crate README.
.\" Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-SPOOL\-EXPORT 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-spool\-export \- move robodr\-agentd findings from its spool into signed one\-way export batches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-spool\-export
.B \-\-spool
.I DIR
.B \-\-outbox
.I DIR
.B \-\-state
.I FILE
.B \-\-pack\-state
.I FILE
.B \-\-unit
.I ID
.B \-\-key\-file
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-key\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-hmac ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-batch\-bytes
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-findings
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-rejected\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-interval\-ms
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-once ]
.RB [ \-\-upgrade\-data\-source
.IR LABEL ]
.RB [ \-\-upgrade\-topic
.IR TOPIC ]
.RB [ \-\-rejected\-max\-age\-s
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-rejected\-max\-count
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-rejected\-max\-bytes
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Robot\-side (low side) exporter. It takes the records in
.IB DIR /ready/
of a
.BR robodr\-agentd (8)
findings spool in name order, re\-validates each finding (OCSF contract),
packs them into one signed
.BR robodr\-diode\-pack (1)
batch per step in the outbox, and renames the records into
.IB DIR /acked/
only after the batch has been committed and renamed into the outbox. An intent
journal in the
.B \-\-state
file makes every crash point recoverable without loss or re\-packing. Records
leave
.I ready/
only by rename, never by deletion: an invalid record is moved to the rejected
directory with a reason file. The rejected directory is kept in full unless
bounded with the
.B \-\-rejected\-max\-*
options.
.PP
Without
.B \-\-once
it runs one step every
.B \-\-interval\-ms
and, after an error, re\-opens the packer and the exporter (which finish a
half\-written batch) and retries. Each step that exported, rejected or
recovered something prints a JSON report on stdout.
.PP
Per\-finding signatures
.RB ( robodr\-finding\-sig ,
contract \(sc2a) are
.B not
carried across the diode: the batch format holds finding values only and is
authenticated by the batch signature.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-spool " DIR"
The agentd spool root (it must be able to rename inside it: run as the
daemon's user).
.TP
.BI \-\-outbox " DIR"
Diode outbox (as \fBrobodr\-diode\-pack \-\-outbox\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-state " FILE"
Exporter state and intent journal.
.TP
.BI \-\-pack\-state " FILE"
Packer state (next batch sequence, last batch hash), as
\fBrobodr\-diode\-pack \-\-state\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-unit " ID"
Unit id written into every manifest.
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-file " FILE"
The unit's diode signing key, a
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1)
secret key file (Ed25519 by default); the same file checks as
.BR robodr\-diode\-pack (1).
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-id " ID"
Key id (default: the key file's).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-hmac
Accept a legacy HMAC\-SHA256 key file (a warning is printed).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-batch\-bytes " N\fR, " \-\-max\-findings " N"
Batch limits, as for
.BR robodr\-diode\-pack (1)
(defaults 16 MiB and 10000).
.TP
.BI \-\-rejected\-dir " DIR"
Where invalid records go (default \fIspool\fB/rejected/\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-rejected\-max\-age\-s " N\fR, " \-\-rejected\-max\-count " N\fR, " \-\-rejected\-max\-bytes " N"
After each run, delete the oldest rejected records (each with its
.B .reason.json
file) older than N seconds, beyond the N newest, or beyond N bytes in all
(0 or absent = no such bound; default: keep everything). A rejected record is
never packed and never read again, so only its forensic copy is lost; a name
that is in
.I ready/
is never touched.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval\-ms " N"
Loop interval, > 0 (default 5000).
.TP
.B \-\-once
One step, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-upgrade\-data\-source " LABEL\fR, " \-\-upgrade\-topic " TOPIC"
An unsigned contract 1.x record (spooled before an upgrade) is upgraded to
contract 2.0 with these labels (defaults
.B robodr
and
.BR robodr.findings ),
keeping its identity. A signed 1.x record is moved to the rejected directory
with the reason "legacy 1.x signed record: re\-sign required".
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.RB ( \-\-once ).
.TP
.B 1
Error with
.B \-\-once
(without it, errors are printed and retried).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SYSTEMD UNIT
The package ships
.B robodr\-spool\-export.service
(installed disabled) for the robot side of a diode site. It runs as user
.B robodr
with no network
.RB ( PrivateNetwork=yes ),
reads
.I /var/lib/robodr/spool/agentd
and writes batches to
.IR /var/lib/robodr/export/diode ,
state under
.IR /var/lib/robodr/export/spool\-export/ .
The key
.I /etc/robodr/keys/diode.key
is handed over as
.IR /run/credentials/robodr\-spool\-export.service/diode.key ;
the unit id and extra flags come from
.I /etc/robodr/spool\-export.env
.RB ( ROBODR_UNIT_ID ,
.BR ROBODR_SPOOL_EXPORT_ARGS ).
It conflicts with
.B robodr\-kafka\-publish.service
(one consumer per spool).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-diode\-pack (1),
.BR robodr\-diode\-unpack (1),
.BR robodr\-kafka\-publish (1),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
